Per-tensor ZP external correction and complete ZP-buffer clock gating
Date: 2026-10-28 (Asia/Shanghai)
Simulator: ModelSim SE 2020.4; actual VCS and physical synthesis/STA were not run.
Final RTL: tensor output = clip_INT8(round(raw * multiplier0 * 2^shift0)).
TB tensor result = clip_INT8(signed(CIM_INT8) + signed(channel_ZP)).
Per-channel retains its original in-CIM ZP addition before saturation.
AS Context ZP and batch ZP reuse existing channel-only clock domains.
Per-tensor actual ZP-clock levels and no-load/hold are checked in Cluster TB.
Unknown unused tensor ZP and cross-Tile changes are accepted; scale checks remain.
All 10 TBs compile normally and under SYNTHESIS conditions.
Final catalogue: 133 PASS, 0 FAIL; 90 expected protocol rejections.
Unit vectors: 17908 full-range scalar cases checked in BOTH modes,
512 four-channel cases, 145312 numeric output checks plus TB correction checks.
All 11 positive GEMM cases check both CIM_INT8 and corrected golden.
Six per-channel matrix/stimulus baselines remain byte-identical numerically.
Negative mutation PASS: reconnecting ZP to active shared clocks is rejected
by the actual-clock checker, despite unchanged no-write enables.
